From 330ee8dd119525b0f4151f4f58d6b228c53f2771 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:37:56 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Make invalid ranges an explicit error, and check replay
 against the text

mutateReplace and friends return MUTATE_INVALID, and bulkDelete and bulkInsert
return -1, with nothing changed.  bulkDelete no longer clamps: its clamped range
disagreed with the record, so undo didn't restore the text.  bulkInsert past a
row was a negative memmove.

Undo and redo now check a record against the text before replaying it, and
report UNDO_MISMATCH rather than corrupt the buffer.  Text can still change
without a record (TAB in a prompt, a writable special buffer being rebuilt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01947MBgCkoERXfoyRGfCmQi
